---
export const title = 'Range';
export const order = 200;
import DemoComponentCard from '../../../../components/DemoComponentCard.astro';
---

<p>
  With <code>range</code> the picker takes two clicks: the first sets the start and fires
  <code>input</code>, the second sets the end and fires <code>change</code>. The ends are put in
  order, so the end can be picked before the start. While the end is being chosen, the band follows
  the pointer. <code>months="2"</code> shows two months side by side.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <wc-date-picker range months='2' value='2026-11-03/2026-11-09'></wc-date-picker>
</DemoComponentCard>

<p>A range value is two ISO dates joined by a slash: <code>2026-11-03/2026-11-09</code>.</p>
